{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-flow","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:q-reeb-flow","kind":"example","title":"$q$-Deformed Reeb flow","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-vector-field"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb","tags":["reeb-flow","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QReebFlow","text":"q-reeb-flow.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-flow.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:q-reeb-flow\"></a><p>In the archimedean realisation, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Reeb vector field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi_q</code> generates a one-parameter family of diffeomorphisms <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\phi_t^q \\colon M \\to M</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\frac{d}{dt}\\phi_t^q =  \\xi_q \\circ \\phi_t^q, \\qquad \\phi_0^q = \\mathrm{id}_M.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-flow.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Example","number":"3.19.5"}
